      ],
      "statement": "For the maps dₜ(a)=(a,ta) into C², some ℤ/q linear combination of the 2e+2 images of the cyclic word is a boundary with a unit among its coefficients.",
      "hypotheses": "As in CYC-01 with q a power of the prime ℓ, t=0,…,2e+1. The generator bound applies to homology with trivial coefficients, as an abelian group.",
      "definitions": [
        "finite free integer cover",
        "long exact sequence",
        "permutation module",
        "Shapiro isomorphism",
        "cycle modulo boundaries"
      ],
      "correspondence": "Two short exact sequences from the cyclic difference map give at most 2e+1 generators in degree 2e. Lifting the classes to a free abelian group permits cancelling the common prime factors before projection. After projection to homology the vanishing combination is represented by a boundary in the bar complex.",
