    {
      "id": "CYC-04",
      "title": "The projective-line transfer reads the determinant",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-projective-transfer",
      "equations": [
        "inputs-residue-block"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "CYC-03"
      ],
      "statement": "For a finite k-vector space V and a gluing automorphism g on a pure scalar weight-x block, the transferred functional evaluates its prism to xᵉv(det g) in ℤ/q.",
      "hypotheses": "Under the assumptions of CYC-03. The finite field has |k|≡1 modulo q because ζ has order q. The source separately handles q=1.",
      "definitions": [
        "projectivization",
        "coefficient transfer",
        "direct sum",
        "elementary shear",
        "determinant"
      ],
      "correspondence": "Line ratios along successive inverse actions define a transfer commuting with boundaries. The two projective fibers in V⊕W have cardinalities |W| and 1, equal modulo q. The prism law gives a homomorphism, and elementary shears have trivial image. Direct sums and the scalar case then determine its value on a diagonal and hence on every invertible matrix.",
